        "message": "#(preaggregate) on measure \"total\" of source \"zoned\" is not built, so the measure is served live: the source sets its own time zone (`timezone: 'America/Los_Angeles'`), and a query on it is never read from a rollup, whose stored times would be read in another zone, nor through a join (no source in the same zone joins it), so its table would cost a build no query reads.",
